  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Should You Keep the Existing Layout During a Primary Bathroom Remodel?",
    "text": "Should You Keep the Existing Layout During a Primary Bathroom Remodel?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "The right choice depends on the room’s existing layout, the condition of plumbing and electrical systems, the desired fixtures, ventilation, storage, accessibility needs, and whether walls or structural elements will change. In San Diego County, homeowners should ask the contractor to explain the local approval path, design documents, inspection points, and how each decision affects scope before construction begins.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "Elite Remodeling & Design",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
